# HOTFIX-008 — Increase Maximum Typing Speed Limit Completion Report

## Executive Summary

**HOTFIX-008** has been successfully implemented, verified across all quality gates (126 unit tests passing), linted cleanly across all static analysis tools, and packaged into the production standalone build (`dist/batmanoverlay/batmanoverlay.exe`).

The maximum configurable human typing speed limit has been expanded from **300 WPM** to **2000 WPM** without introducing artificial throttling, hidden safety caps, or internal speed clamping. Backward compatibility for all existing settings (`60 WPM`, `120 WPM`, `250 WPM`, `300 WPM`) remains 100% intact.

---

## Technical Changes

1. **`TypingConfig` Model (`src/typing/config.py`)**:
   - Expanded Pydantic field validator for `speed_wpm` to allow range $[20.0, 2000.0]$ WPM.
   - Preserved default WPM at $60.0$ WPM.
2. **Typing UI Control Panel (`src/ui/typing_panel.py`)**:
   - Updated `_spin_wpm` (QSpinBox) range to `(20, 2000)`.
   - Updated `_slider_wpm` (QSlider) range to `(20, 2000)`.
3. **Automated Test Suite (`tests/unit/test_typing_engine.py` & `tests/unit/test_typing_panel.py`)**:
   - Added `test_typing_config_high_speed_wpm_limit` asserting validation of 2000 WPM, duration calculation at high WPM, legacy WPM backward compatibility, and out-of-bounds rejection ($> 2000$ WPM).
   - Added SpinBox and Slider range assertions in `test_typing_panel_initialization`.

